  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an undirected tree with NNN nodes and N−1N-1N−1 edges, where each node is colored either red or blue, define two sets S1S_1S1​ and S2S_2S2​ as follows:\n\n\nS1={dis(u,v)∣1≤u&lt;v≤N}S_1 = \\{dis(u,v) \\mid 1 \\leq u \\lt v \\leq N\\}S1​={dis(u,v)∣1≤u&lt;v≤N}\nS2={dis(u,v)∣1≤u&lt;v≤N,coloru≠colorv}S_2 = \\{dis(u,v) \\mid 1 \\leq u \\lt v \\leq N, color_u \\neq color_v\\}S2​={dis(u,v)∣1≤u&lt;v≤N,coloru​=colorv​} ,\n\nwhere dis(u,v)=dis(u,v) = dis(u,v)= number of edges on the simple path between uuu and vvv.\n**Note:** Sets S1S_1S1​ and S2S_2S2​ only contain **distinct** elements.\n\nWe call the coloring good if S1=S2S_1 = S_2S1​=S2​.\n\nLet CRC_RCR​ and CBC_BCB​ denote the number of nodes that are colored red and blue respectively.\n\nGiven an undirected tree with NNN nodes and N−1N-1N−1 edges, find a good coloring of the tree such that the value of ∣CR−CB∣|C_R - C_B|∣CR​−CB​∣ is **minimized**.\n\nIt can be shown that a good coloring always exists. If there are multiple good colorings with the minimum value of ∣CR−CB∣|C_R - C_B|∣CR​−CB​∣, you may output any of them.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the number of vertices of the tree.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges of the tree. The ithi^{th}ith of these N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between nodes uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a string SSS of length NNN, where Si=RS_i = RSi​=R if node iii is colored red or Si=BS_i = BSi​=B if node iii is colored blue.\n\n\nNote that string SSS should represent a good coloring of the tree such that the value of ∣CR−CB∣|C_R - C_B|∣CR​−CB​∣ is **minimized**.\n\n\nIf there are multiple good colorings with the minimum value of ∣CR−CB∣|C_R - C_B|∣CR​−CB​∣, you may output any possible string.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤20002 \\leq N \\leq 20002≤N≤2000",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The edges in the input form a tree.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 200020002000."
    ],
